<p>A thumbnail is read in a grid of strangers’ thumbnails at about 300 pixels wide. What survives that: two lines of big type, one accent, one face, one picture, one word in the hand. What does not: a line of small text, three colours, a logo in the middle. Below, all ten styles at grid size, four a row, mixed the way a channel mixes them.</p>
